<title>PHILIPPINES: New Zealand firm eyes Manila power plant rehab.</title>
<headline>New Zealand firm eyes Manila power plant rehab.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asia Power of New Zealand is vying for a 25-year contract to rehabilitate and maintain the 350-megawatt Caliraya-Botocan-Kalayaan hydroelectric power plant in the northern Philippines, a National Power Corp official said on Monday.</p>
<p>Asia Power has written to the NPC expressing its interest in challenging a bid by Industries Mettalurgica Pescarmona S.A. of Argentina, which submitted an unsolicited proposal for the rehabilitation of the power plant, the official said.</p>
<p>Under Philippine government bidding rules, companies can submit proposals to match an unsolicited bid.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 fax 8176267</p>
